// Tower Pro SG90, the 9 g micro servo in Arduino starter kits. The mechanical travel the
// model follows is the measured 0.5 ms at 0° to 2.4 ms at 180°. The Luxorparts sheet says
// 1 ms is 0°, 1.5 ms is 90° and 2 ms is 180°. Tower Pro's page gives the 4.8 V speed and the
// 1 µs dead band. Luxorparts gives that speed and 0.10 s per 60° at 6 V. SunFounder's SF0180
// specification gives the currents. The control board is an AA51880, which states no
// operating supply range. 4tronix lists 3.0 V to 7.2 V, the lowest such minimum cited.
// The shape follows Tower Pro's SG90 drawing: a 22.2 x 11.8 mm case, ears 32.2 mm end to end
// with their underside 16 mm up, and 31 mm to the top of the horn. The lead ends in a 3-pin
// female connector, so the servo stands beside the breadboard and jumpers reach its pins.
